<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $97 mln Jan 9.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $97 mln Jan 9.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $97 million surplus on Jan 9 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON JANUARY 9</p>
<p>Exports: $234.2 million</p>
<p>Imports: $188.4 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $378.6 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $327.4 million</p>
<p>Surplus: $97 million</p>
<p>JANUARY DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $1.193 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $1.338 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $1.567 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $1.227 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $195 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>((-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-2485418))</p>
